{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception capabilities, separating sensor outcomes (uncontrollable) from motion commands (controllable). The specification enforces safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are used only when obstacles are detected. Recovery is conservative but not excessive; full_rotate is reserved for repeated or ambiguous blockages. The supervisor quickly returns to exploration after recovery, avoids oscillation, and never enables forward or random_walk in obstacle states.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to reflect open-loop actuation and asynchronous sensing.",
    "Specification automaton encodes the exploration policy: prefer random_walk in clear, move_forward in commit, use short turns for recovery, and only use full_rotate as a last resort. All obstacle states force a recovery turn before returning to exploration."
  ],
